+.. pp:param:: <collision_name>.ionization_secondary_energy_scale
+    :type: ``float``
+    :optional:
+
+    Only for ``background_mcc`` with ``ionization``. If positive, the energy :math:`W` of the
+    ejected electron is drawn from :math:`1/(W^2 + \bar{w}^2)` on
+    :math:`[0, (E - E_{ion})/2]`, with :math:`\bar{w}` this value in eV
+    (`Opal et al., J. Chem. Phys. 55, 4100 (1971) <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1676707>`__),
+    the ejected electron is emitted isotropically, and the incident electron keeps its
+    direction and the remaining energy.
+    By default the two electrons share the energy equally and both are scattered isotropically.
+
 .. pp:param:: <collision_name>.ionization_target_species
     :type: ``string``
 
